{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"500b7841a69df1cb","name":"card_unit_big_red_one","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BloodIron/units/card_unit_big_red_one","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BIG RED ONE","text":"Cards in your hand cost 4 kredits.","flavorText":"The 1st Infantry Division, known for its iconic red \"1\" insignia and nicknamed \"The Big Red One\", was one of the most distinguished and experienced U.S. divisions in WWII. The division saw action in some of the most crucial battles in both North Africa and Europe. Its WWII service began in 1942 in North Africa with Operation Torch , where it engaged in fierce fighting against Vichy France troops, and the Tunisian Campaign against German and Italian forces. After the Allies successfully pushed the Axis out of North Africa, the 1st Infantry Division participated in Operation Husky, the Allied invasion of Sicily, in 1943. One of the division’s most famous roles came on D-Day, June 6, 1944, when it led the assault on Omaha Beach during the Normandy invasion. Despite facing intense German resistance and heavy casualties, the Big Red One ultimately secured the beachhead. The division kept fighting through France and Belgium, and was involved in the brutal Battle of the Hürtgen Forest, and later the Battle of the Bulge, helping to repel the last major German offensive in the Ardennes forest. At the end of the war, the Big Red One fought through Germany, liberating towns and concentration camps until the final victory in Europe.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":8,"operationCost":4,"attack":8,"defense":8},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_big_red_one","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_big_red_one_title","SourceString":"BIG RED ONE","LocalizedString":"BIG RED ONE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":8,"defense":8,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":8,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_big_red_one_text","SourceString":"Cards in your hand cost 4 kredits.","LocalizedString":"Cards in your hand cost 4 kredits."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_big_red_one_history","SourceString":"The 1st Infantry Division, known for its iconic red \"1\" insignia and nicknamed \"The Big Red One\", was one of the most distinguished and experienced U.S. divisions in WWII. The division saw action in some of the most crucial battles in both North Africa and Europe. Its WWII service began in 1942 in North Africa with Operation Torch , where it engaged in fierce fighting against Vichy France troops, and the Tunisian Campaign against German and Italian forces. After the Allies successfully pushed the Axis out of North Africa, the 1st Infantry Division participated in Operation Husky, the Allied invasion of Sicily, in 1943. One of the division’s most famous roles came on D-Day, June 6, 1944, when it led the assault on Omaha Beach during the Normandy invasion. Despite facing intense German resistance and heavy casualties, the Big Red One ultimately secured the beachhead. The division kept fighting through France and Belgium, and was involved in the brutal Battle of the Hürtgen Forest, and later the Battle of the Bulge, helping to repel the last major German offensive in the Ardennes forest. At the end of the war, the Big Red One fought through Germany, liberating towns and concentration camps until the final victory in Europe.","LocalizedString":"The 1st Infantry Division, known for its iconic red \"1\" insignia and nicknamed \"The Big Red One\", was one of the most distinguished and experienced U.S. divisions in WWII. The division saw action in some of the most crucial battles in both North Africa and Europe. Its WWII service began in 1942 in North Africa with Operation Torch , where it engaged in fierce fighting against Vichy France troops, and the Tunisian Campaign against German and Italian forces. After the Allies successfully pushed the Axis out of North Africa, the 1st Infantry Division participated in Operation Husky, the Allied invasion of Sicily, in 1943. One of the division’s most famous roles came on D-Day, June 6, 1944, when it led the assault on Omaha Beach during the Normandy invasion. Despite facing intense German resistance and heavy casualties, the Big Red One ultimately secured the beachhead. The division kept fighting through France and Belgium, and was involved in the brutal Battle of the Hürtgen Forest, and later the Battle of the Bulge, helping to repel the last major German offensive in the Ardennes forest. At the end of the war, the Big Red One fought through Germany, liberating towns and concentration camps until the final victory in Europe."},"operationCost":4,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSpawnedInHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardSuppressed"],"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/Winter_2024/t_big_red_one.t_big_red_one","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Top","artist":"US WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/BIG_RED_ONE.BIG_RED_ONE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":406.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_big_red_one_photo","SourceString":"Soldiers of the 1st Infantry Division crossing the Weser River in assault boats to take Fürstenberg in Germany. 8 April 1945.","LocalizedString":"Soldiers of the 1st Infantry Division crossing the Weser River in assault boats to take Fürstenberg in Germany. 8 April 1945."},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Explosions/Large/Infantry/P_ExplosionInfantryL.154"